# These belong to the PySide6 desktop app, not the web deployment.
# Vercel's build step auto-installs a root-level requirements.txt (that's
# where pyside6-essentials/pyside6-addons/numpy/pandas/matplotlib were
# coming from, blowing the Python function bundle past 500MB) - excluding
# it here stops Vercel from ever seeing it.
#
# Every pattern below is anchored with a leading "/" on purpose: gitignore
# syntax (which .vercelignore follows) matches an unanchored pattern like
# "main.py" at ANY depth, which silently also excluded api/app/main.py,
# api/app/config.py, api/requirements.txt, and frontend/dist/assets/ -
# breaking the actual web app. Anchoring restricts each pattern to the
# repo root only, where the desktop app's own files live.
/requirements.txt
/main.py
/config.py
/ui/
/auth/
/database/
/utils/
/tests/
/assets/
/.github/
/venv/
/backups/
/exports/
/logs/
/reports/
